    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class, and it passes green. \n\nThe change is complete. Here's what I implemented for the `membershipNumber` feature (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`, e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`):\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a persisted `membershipNumber` field (`@Column(name = \"membership_number\")`) with getter/setter, matching the existing `customerCode`/`namesakeCount` pattern so it's returned unchanged on later GET reads.\n\n2. **New function** (`rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerMembershipNumber.java`) \u2014 reads the owner via `@Val`, computes `customerCode + \"-M\" + <last two digits of registrationDate year>` (zero-padded to two digits), and sets it in place.\n\n3. **POST pipeline** (`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`) \u2014 inserted the `assignMembershipNumber` step (under `transaction` governance) after `assignCustomerCode` and after `defaultRegistrationDate`, so both required inputs are already set before it runs.\n\n4. **OpenAPI schema** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added the read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name automatically.\n\n5. **DB schema** \u2014 added a `membership_number VARCHAR(30)` column to the `hsqldb` schema (used by the tests) and `h2` schema, and appended the matching 12th `NULL` value to the positional seed inserts in `db/hsqldb/data.sql`.\n\nThe test derives the expected value from the owner's own returned `customerCode` and `registrationDate`, and it passes green along with the full suite (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
